I got big hopes for her.

263
00:14:07,630 --> 00:14:12,260
She's gonna be a doctor or a realtor.

264
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:17,890
Wow, Frank. Ha. I think we just ran out of kids.

265
00:14:19,140 --> 00:14:21,150
Oh, I think you're right.

266
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:28,780
Oh, wow. Phoebe, I don't think I can give one of them up.

267
00:14:28,950 --> 00:14:32,700
I mean, you know, they drive me crazy, but they're my babies.

268
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:38,500
I'm sorry, Frank, I didn't realize things were so bad.

269
00:14:38,660 --> 00:14:41,920
You know, I'll help out more. I can babysit anytime you want.

270
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:43,750
You name the day and I'll be there.

271
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:46,300
How about tomorrow?

272
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:46,300
Well, that's not good.

273
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:50,170
But I can move some stuff around and I'll be there.

274
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:52,800
You and Alice just take the whole day together.

275
00:14:52,970 --> 00:14:55,010
Tsk. You'd do that for us?

276
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:57,470
Are you kidding? That's what sisters are for.

277
00:14:58,730 --> 00:15:00,770
Tsk. Oh.

278
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:05,980
Oh, look at them.

279
00:15:06,150 --> 00:15:09,780
Oh. I love you so much.

280
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:13,490
Oh, crap, don't wake up! Don't wake up!

281
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:19,540
Where are Bill and Colleen?

282
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:19,540
Kitchen, getting something to eat.

283
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:22,790
Can you believe how nice they are?

284
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:22,790
We have to leave.

285
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:27,300
Why? What did you do in the bathroom?

286
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:30,380
I didn't get to the bathroom. I bumped into Owen on the way.

287
00:15:30,550 --> 00:15:33,260
He didn't know he was adopted. There's a slight chance...

288
00:15:33,430 --> 00:15:34,760
...I may have told him.

289
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:38,430
Oh, my God, where's my purse? No, I can replace everything in there.

290
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:41,600
Get that binder and let's go!

291
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:41,600
Hi. Ha.

292
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:43,730
Some little snacks for everybody.

293
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:46,270
You don't have to eat the sour worms. Those are for Owen.

294
00:15:47,650 --> 00:15:49,030
COLLEEN: I'll get him in a second.

295
00:15:49,190 --> 00:15:52,530
Uh, by the way, you should know, we haven't told him he's adopted yet.

296
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:55,410
But kids are so intuitive.

297
00:15:55,570 --> 00:15:57,910
Don't you think, on some level, he already knows?

298
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:01,450
I'm adopted?

299
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:01,450
See? Intuitive.

300
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,040
What? Where did you hear that?

301
00:16:04,210 --> 00:16:05,330
He told me.

302
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,510
And he paid me 50 dollars not to tell.

303
00:16:11,090 --> 00:16:13,720
Which, technically, now you should give back.

304
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:18,640
You told him he's adopted?

305
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:21,560
I'm sorry. You should have a sign out there or something.

306
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:24,850
Or at least whisper it to people when they come in the door.

307
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:26,850
"Owen doesn't know he's adopted...

308
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,560
...and he also thinks Santa is real."

309
00:16:28,730 --> 00:16:30,480
He isn't?

310
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:34,030
We have to get out of here, baby.

311
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:40,660
Everyone, I would like to make a toast...

312
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:43,790
...to Rachel and Joey.

313
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:48,790
And to love.

314
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,880
Ah, love!

315
00:16:53,050 --> 00:16:54,760
Mm.

316
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:57,300
L-O-V-E. Love.

317
00:16:57,470 --> 00:16:59,600
L is for "life."

318
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:02,350
And what is life without love?

319
00:17:03,350 --> 00:17:04,930
Oh, my God, are we supposed to answer?

320
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:10,730
O is for:

321
00:17:11,690 --> 00:17:13,820
"Oh, wow!"

322
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:20,370
The V is for this...

323
00:17:20,530 --> 00:17:24,540
...very surprising turn of events...

324
00:17:24,830 --> 00:17:28,420
...which I am still fine with, by the way.

325
00:17:30,210 --> 00:17:32,300
E...

326
00:17:35,090 --> 00:17:36,880
is for how...

327
00:17:37,050 --> 00:17:41,010
...extremely normal I find it...

328
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:43,310
...that you two...

329
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,770
...are together.

330
00:17:47,850 --> 00:17:51,480
And that one day you might get married...

331
00:17:53,730 --> 00:17:56,650
...and have children of your own.

332
00:18:00,530 --> 00:18:03,830
Dude, are you okay?

333
00:18:00,530 --> 00:18:03,830
Totally.

334
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:07,210
Ross, you don't seem okay.

335
00:18:07,370 --> 00:18:09,540
I'm sorry, it must be the pressure of entertaining.

336
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:18,090
I think everyone would feel better if we had some flan.

337
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:21,890
Wait, Ross. Ross, I, um... I have to take off.

338
00:18:22,050 --> 00:18:23,890
No!

339
00:18:22,050 --> 00:18:23,890
I'm sorry.

340
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:26,720
I have an early class in the morning.

341
00:18:26,890 --> 00:18:30,310
But this has been lovely.

342
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:35,150
Wasn't it? And you thought it would be awkward with Joey.

343
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,650
And that you never really liked Rachel.

344
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:43,070
You are on fire! I'll call you in the morning, okay?

345
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,910
Okay.

346
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,910
All right.

347
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:50,120
Rachel, what Ross just said, that's just...

348
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:53,500
Oh, that's okay. Girls tend not to like me.

349
00:18:53,670 --> 00:18:55,420
Fine.

350
00:18:57,550 --> 00:19:01,300
Okay. I guess it's just flan for three.

351
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:03,140
Hey.

352
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:05,350
Hey, that rhymes.

353
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:10,690
You know what, Ross, I think, uh, we're gonna take off too.

354
00:19:10,850 --> 00:19:15,820
Oh, oh. Heh. Of course. God, I'm so stupid.

355
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:17,530
You guys are a couple now.

356
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:20,150
I mean, you probably just want to be alone.

357
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:23,990
No, it's just getting late...

358
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:23,990
It's fine. It's totally fine.

359
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:27,120
I've got plenty of margaritas. It's all good.

360
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:36,130
I don't even know what that's for.

361
00:19:41,550 --> 00:19:43,220
You know what?

362
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:46,510
I think I'm gonna stay here and make sure he's okay.

363
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:49,100
That's probably a good idea.

364
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:49,100
I'll see you in the morning.

365
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:51,850
Uh-huh. Okay.

366
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:51,850
All right.

367
00:19:52,270 --> 00:19:53,850
Yeah, you know, Joey, I...

368
00:19:54,020 --> 00:19:57,480
I don't think he's ever gonna be okay with this.

369
00:19:57,650 --> 00:20:00,150
It doesn't look good, does it?

370
00:19:57,650 --> 00:20:00,150
Mm-mm.

371
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,300
Morning.

372
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:24,340
Here you go.

373
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:24,340
Thanks.

374
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:28,300
Did you stay here all night?

375
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:28,300
Yeah.

376
00:20:29,810 --> 00:20:32,930
So you took off my pants and shoes?

377
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,810
No. No, no.

378
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:39,020
You actually did that when you were dancing to the Chicago soundtrack.

379
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:44,360
Ahem. Look, uh, Ross...

380
00:20:44,530 --> 00:20:47,990
...about Rachel and I. Listen, you don't have to worry about that...

381
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:50,370
...because nothing's gonna happen.

382
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:51,790
What do you mean?

383
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,250
She and I said from the beginning...

384
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:58,330
...we weren't gonna do anything unless you were okay with it.

385
00:20:58,500 --> 00:20:59,880
And clearly...

386
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:02,800
What are you talking about? I'm fine.

387
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:06,930
It's okay, Ross. You know, I totally understand.

388
00:21:07,090 --> 00:21:09,050
Of course you're not fine. You're...

389
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,600
You're Ross and Rachel.

390
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:18,100
Yeah, except we're not.

391
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:22,440
I mean, we haven't been a couple in, like...

392
00:21:24,110 --> 00:21:26,610
...six years.

393
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:30,950
My God, is that right?

394
00:21:31,450 --> 00:21:32,740
Has it been that long?

395
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:36,120
That's what I hear, yeah.

396
00:21:37,620 --> 00:21:41,420
This is crazy. I mean, six years...

397
00:21:41,590 --> 00:21:44,880
...and because of me, you guys aren't gonna be together?

398
00:21:46,170 --> 00:21:48,220
Can I ask you something?

399
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,840
Really...

400
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:53,180
...what is this thing with you and Rachel?

401
00:21:55,430 --> 00:21:59,100
Come on, you know me. Ha, ha. You know...

402
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,400
Joey.

403
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:10,320
I'm crazy about her.

404
00:22:15,410 --> 00:22:18,210
And she feels the same way?

405
00:22:20,170 --> 00:22:22,250
I think so.

406
00:22:24,670 --> 00:22:26,340
Well, then...

407
00:22:26,510 --> 00:22:28,720
...maybe it's time we all moved on.

408
00:22:29,300 --> 00:22:31,890
Yeah, but, Ross, I mean, you're not okay with it, so...

409
00:22:32,050 --> 00:22:35,140
No, but I want to be.

410
00:22:35,310 --> 00:22:37,140
And hey:

411
00:22:37,310 --> 00:22:39,020
I will be.

412
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:44,820
Besides, I'm with Charlie, right?

413
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:47,490
Oh, my God, I'm still with Charlie, aren't I?

414
00:22:47,650 --> 00:22:50,240
She didn't see the dance, did she?

415
00:22:47,650 --> 00:22:50,240
No, no, no.

416
00:22:51,450 --> 00:22:55,080
No, that was, uh... That was just for me.

417
00:22:58,790 --> 00:23:00,580
Hey, you, uh?

418
00:23:00,750 --> 00:23:02,540
You sure about this?

419
00:23:02,710 --> 00:23:05,420
Yeah, I'm sure.

420
00:23:07,710 --> 00:23:09,170
And...

421
00:23:10,130 --> 00:23:12,010
...we're okay?

422
00:23:23,810 --> 00:23:25,150
Hey, Pheebs.

423
00:23:23,810 --> 00:23:25,150
Hey.

424
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:27,480
Um, we just want to give you a heads up.

425
00:23:27,650 --> 00:23:29,610
Bill and Colleen hate us.

426
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:32,150
Owen didn't know he's adopted and Monica told him.

427
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:33,490
What?

428
00:23:33,660 --> 00:23:35,870
Still, he had to find out sometime.

429
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:40,250
How would you like it if someone told the triplets that you gave birth to them?

430
00:23:44,630 --> 00:23:47,130
I'm gonna go tell Emma she was an accident.

